      "writtenOn": "2021-02-03T17:49:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like, compared to usb_mux_set_safe_mode, this function will:\n1) Put the mux in low-power mode (by disconnecting USB 2.0 charging),\n2) Set mux mode NONE even if the virtual mux is in use, and\n3) Not do anything with PPC-controlled SBU lines.\n\nWhat is the significance of putting the mux into low-power mode and out of it again during the exit sequence?\n\nThe spec says we should enter Safe Mode before sending Exit Mode. Does this violate that, or is there more nuance to the mux modes?\n\nIt looks like this change will bypass the mux set/ack sequence in the virtual mux driver, where previously that would have happened both when transitioning from DP mode to safe mode and from safe mode to USB mode. What is the significance of that?\n\nWhat is the significance of potentially not isolating the PPC lines?",
      "revId": "665754c504fa4e0cf67bb9928e683286aaa44f7e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "553290a4_43b99d44",
        "filename": "common/usb_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 473,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-05T22:26:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At present, PMC/IPC doesn\u0027t support Alt mode-\u003e safe-\u003e USB. So, the only way to get out of an alt mode is to disconnect -\u003e USB-\u003e safe-\u003e alt mode -- More info about this in comment #45 and #48 of the cross-bug.\n\nI don\u0027t think we are particularly violating the spec - We are using a different path to exit.\n\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2632551 - takes care if we miss the disconnect on AP side - and so, we won\u0027t need ACK for disconnect\n\nAdded a new patch set for not coming in and out of LPM and isolating the PPC lines.",
      "parentUuid": "a29ce82d_5488b27f",
      "revId": "665754c504fa4e0cf67bb9928e683286aaa44f7e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
